From 57812fe692e472b96dbc1d8f5a7b423c39ad0090 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:16:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Make the arcade playable by finger, not just keyboard

The games were reachable on a phone but not really playable: canvas
coordinates ignored the CSS scale factor, the play field ran off the
bottom of the viewport, and the shared control pad carried whatever
labels the previous game left on it.

Shared touch engine
- canvasPos() converts pointers through the canvas scale factor. On a
  340px-wide board a raw clientX-rect.left reported x=340 into a 400-wide
  play field, so every game silently lost the right ~15% of its width.
- bindCanvasDrag() gives one pointer path (mouse/touch/stylus) with
  pointer capture, so a drag survives the finger leaving the canvas.
- fitCanvas() scales the board to the space actually left after the
  header, progress bar and pad, preserving aspect ratio and capped at 1x
  so desktop stays pixel-exact. Re-runs on resize and orientation change.
- setControls() has each game declare its own pad; setControlHint() and
  the #touch-hint overlay state the gesture rather than the keybind.

Per-game controls
- Neon Nebula: hold anywhere to fire, drag to fly. Firing runs off the
  same weapon cooldown as Space, so touch gets no tap-spam edge. The ship
  gained a vertical band, and W/S/Up/Down on keyboard to match.
- Dodge Cores: relative drag - the dot tracks how far the finger moves
  rather than snapping under it, so your thumb doesn't cover the gap
  you're aiming for.
- Cyberpunk Tetris: hard-drop button, plus drag to slide, pull to soft
  drop, flick to slam and tap to rotate. Arrows auto-repeat on hold.
- Cyber Arena: drag plants a virtual stick and moves; tap slashes toward
  the tap; double-tap deploys the ability. Pad becomes DASH / ABILITY.
- Pong drags the paddle, Snake takes swipes, Flappy taps through one
  pointerdown path instead of click + touchstart firing twice.
- Reaction Time is timed on pointerdown; waiting for the synthesised
  click was adding latency to the one number the game scores.

Layout
- Hub shows two compact game cards per row instead of eleven
  screen-tall ones; blurbs clamp so cards line up.
- Landscape moves the pad beside the board and drops the header hint,
  which nearly doubles the board on a 390px-tall viewport.
- Hover lift/glow is disabled where there's no hover - tapping latched
  it on and left cards floating.

Verified with Playwright across iPhone SE/12 portrait, both landscapes
and tablet: aspect ratio held, nothing clipped, no horizontal overflow,
no page errors, and desktop unchanged at a native 400x500.

